  "texts": {
    "preamble": "D.Muthupandi vs The Commissioner on 25 March, 2024 Author: G.R.Swaminathan Bench: G.R.Swaminathan W.P(MD)No.5805 of 20 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 25.03.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice G.R.Swaminathan W.P(MD)No.5805 of 2024 and W.M.P(MD)No.5472 of 2024 D.Muthupandi ...",
    "facts": "2.The petitioner's shop has been sealed for breach of FSSAI Act. This is because the Hon'ble Division Bench is seized of the matter and an interim order has https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis also been granted in the appeal filed by the State. The petitioner's shop was sealed on 14.02.2024. More than a month has elapsed.",
    "arguments": "3.The learned Additional Advocate General points out that the petitioner after given a solemn undertaking before this Court had breached the same and that therefore the writ petition deserves dismissal. The petitioner is warned that if he is caught again, he may lose the license to conduct his business even. The learned Additional Advocate General also informs this Court that the petitioner's registration has been cancelled.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3.The learned Additional Advocate General points out that the petitioner after given a solemn undertaking before this Court had breached the same and that therefore the writ petition deserves dismissal. The petitioner is warned that if he is caught again, he may lose the license to conduct his business even. The learned Additional Advocate General also informs this Court that the petitioner's registration has been cancelled.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
